{red|**Take a moment to honestly name what you have lost or are losing in this journey.**

What dreams have been delayed or shattered?}{red| What grief have you been carrying that no one else sees?}{red| What emotions have you been pushing down or hiding?}

**Write openly about your losses.** No one else needs to read this. Let yourself be honest:

{red|**Think about how your spouse has been grieving.**

How does their grief show up?}{red| What do they do when they are hurting?}

{red|How is their grief style different from yours?}

{red|Have there been times when their different grief response felt hurtful to you, even though they were not trying to hurt you?}

{red|What do you think they actually need, even if they express it differently than you would?}

Write your observations about your spouse's grief:

{red|What decisions are you currently facing or anticipating in your infertility journey?}

{red|Where do you and your spouse see things similarly?}{red| Where do you see things differently?}{red| What fears or values are driving your perspective?}{red| What do you need to understand better about your spouse's perspective?}

Write about where you are in your decision-making process:

{red|**Reflect honestly on how infertility has affected your intimate life.**

How has the pressure changed your experience of sex?}{red| What emotions come up for you around intimacy now?}{red| What do you miss about how things used to be?}{red| What do you need that you have not been asking for?}

Write openly about the impact on your intimacy:

{red|**Think about the social situations that have been hardest for you.**

What comments or questions hurt the most?}{red| What situations do you dread?}{red| How have you typically responded, and how has that worked?}{red| What do you wish people understood?}

Write about your most challenging interactions:

{red|Create a plan together for handling social challenges:

What is our standard response to 'when are you having kids?}{red|' questions?}

{red|Who are the safe people we can be honest with?}

{red|What events or situations do we need to approach carefully?}

{red|How will we support each other when one of us is struggling socially?}

{red|How will we handle pregnancy announcements from people close to us?}

**Write down your agreed-upon approaches.**

{red|Infertility raises hard spiritual questions:

Why would God withhold something so good?}{red| Is He punishing me for something?}{red| Does He hear my prayers?}{red| Why does He give babies to people who do not want them while withholding from us?}{red| Can I trust a God who allows this pain?}{red| What did I do wrong?}{red| Is there something wrong with my faith?}

**These questions can feel dangerous to ask.** But they are not evidence of weak faith. They are the cries of a heart in pain, and God is big enough to handle them.

{red|If you could say anything to God about your infertility journey, with complete honesty and no filter, what would you say?}

{red|What questions do you have for Him?}{red| What emotions are you feeling toward Him?}{red| What do you need from Him?}

Write your honest prayer:

{red|**Honestly assess how your marriage is doing in the midst of infertility.**

What is going well?}{red| Where are you staying connected?}

{red|What is concerning?}{red| Where do you see strain?}

{red|What does your spouse need from you right now that you have not been giving?}

{red|What do you need from them that you have not been asking for?}

Write your honest assessment:

{red|**Together, make a commitment to protect your marriage through this journey.**

Discuss and agree:

How will we stay connected beyond fertility issues?}

{red|How will we handle disagreements about the journey?}

{red|What will we do if we see our marriage struggling?}

**Finish this sentence together: 'No matter what happens with fertility, we commit to.**..'

**Write your commitment and sign it together.**

{red|If you are considering alternative paths, explore these questions together:

Regarding adoption or foster care: Are we both genuinely drawn to this path?}{red| What type of adoption fits us (domestic, international, foster)?}{red| Are we prepared for the unique challenges adopted children may face?}{red| What are our expectations about birth family involvement?}

{red|Regarding donor options: How do we feel about using genetic material that is not ours?}{red| How would we handle questions from our child about their origins?}{red| What boundaries would we set?}

{red|Regarding living child-free: Can we envision a fulfilling life without children?}{red| What would give our lives meaning and purpose?}{red| How do we feel about this path honestly, not just as resignation?}

{red|**Reflect honestly on alternative paths to parenthood.**

Which options feel open to you?}{red| Which feel closed?}{red| What emotions come up when you consider adoption, donor options, or living child-free?}{red| What fears or concerns do you have about any of these paths?}{red| Where are you and your spouse potentially not aligned?}

Write about your honest feelings regarding alternative paths:

{red|**Reflect on your life beyond infertility.**

What parts of your life have been neglected while focusing on fertility?}

{red|What brings you joy and meaning outside of the hope for children?}

{red|What would it look like to live a full, meaningful life even if children never come?}

{red|What do you want your life to be about beyond your fertility status?}

Write about your life beyond infertility:

{red|What is the most important thing you have learned or been reminded of through this journey?}

{red|What do you want to remember and hold onto going forward?}

Write your key insight:

{red|Based on what you have learned, what does your spouse most need from you as you continue this journey together?}

{red|How can you better support them?}{red| What will you do differently?}

